+**Formulas:**
+The ray equation is $P(t) = O + t \cdot D$, where $O$ is the ray origin, $D$ is the direction, and $t$ is the distance along the ray [G]. The 3D texture is sampled at $V = \text{Texture3D}(P(t))$ [S1]. Front-to-back compositing (mathematically equivalent to the hardware's back-to-front rasterization) updates the accumulated color $C$ and alpha $\alpha$ as:
+$$C_{out} = C_{in} + (1 - \alpha_{in}) \cdot C_{tex} \cdot \alpha_{tex}$$
+$$\alpha_{out} = \alpha_{in} + (1 - \alpha_{in}) \cdot \alpha_{tex}$$
+where $C_{tex}$ and $\alpha_{tex}$ are the sampled color and alpha values [G].
 
